BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Toronto Events (Tockify)
UID:TKF/6755f42da02aaf1c2599e7ae/25048/29907000/0/0
DTSTART:20261111T180000Z
DTEND:20261111T200000Z
URL:https://tockify.com/torevent/detail/25048/1794420000000
SUMMARY: Clothing Conversations
DESCRIPTION:Led by Toronto-based fashion anthropologist Marium Durrani\, 
 Clothing Conversations invites you to a series of three unique workshops 
 bring a meaningful piece of clothing\, textile\, or fabric-based wearable
  and explore the memories\, relationships\, and personal histories connec
 ted to it.\n\n\nSession 01 Wednesday\, November 11\n\nUNRAVEL | Where Our
  Stories Begin\n\n\nSession 02 Wednesday\, November 25\n\nWEAVE | The Peo
 ple & Memories We Carry\n\n\nSession 03 Wednesday\, December 9\n\nTAPESTR
 Y | The Clothes That Tell Our Story\n\nThe first of three unique sessions
 \, UNRAVEL explores where our stories begin and the experiences that shap
 e who we become. From childhood memories\, family traditions\, and cultur
 al heritage to moments of change\, transition\, and new chapters in our l
 ives\, we’ll reflect on the personal histories connected to the things we
  wear and keep.\n\nHOW IT WORKS\n\nBring one meaningful piece of clothing
 \, textile\, or fabric-based wearable. It might be something you wear oft
 en\, a treasured keepsake\, an item passed down through your family\, or 
 something that reminds you of a particular moment. There’s no right or wr
 ong choice—what matters is that it means something to you.\n\nWe’ll begin
  with guided reflection using a Clothing Conversations Memory Tag\, with 
 questions tailored to the session theme. You’ll have a chance to explore 
 your item’s story before deciding what\, if anything\, you’d like to shar
 e.\n\nMarium will facilitate a small storytelling circle where participan
 ts can share and listen to one another. Sharing is always an invitation\,
  never an obligation. During the session\, Marium will photograph your it
 em. Afterward\, she’ll create a personalized digital Garment Card featuri
 ng a photograph of your garment and a summary of its story.\n\nYOUR EXPER
 IENCE INCLUDES\n\n  * A small\, guided storytelling circle\, unique to ea
 ch session\n  * A theme-specific Clothing Conversations Memory Tag for re
 flection\n  * A personalized digital Garment Card featuring your item’s p
 hotograph and a summary of its story\n  * Freshly brewed organic herbal t
 ea from Helen + Hildegard\n\n\nEVENT DETAILS\n\nDate: Wednesday\, Novembe
 r 11\, 2026\n\nTime: 1:00pm – 3:00pm\n\nLocation: HELEN + HILDEGARD | 780
  St Clair Ave W\n\nTickets: Sliding-scale tickets from $20 to $50\, tax i
 ncluded\n\nPlease arrive within 15 minutes of the ticket time to allow fo
 r a moment to settle in.
CATEGORIES:Storytelling
