SUMMARY: Kosher Kabob: A Comedy Show
DESCRIPTION:The Jewish Comedy Festival presents Kosher Kabob: A Comedy Sh
 ow\, a night of stand-up served hot off the grill.\n\nFive of Toronto's s
 harpest comics take the stage at The Boardroom Comedy Club for 90 minutes
  of stand-up about family\, food\, guilt\, dating\, and everything in bet
 ween. Host Brandon Zakkai leads a lineup featuring Kristin Doucet\, Ronen
  Geisler and Oleg Redko\, with headliner Faraz Niafattah closing out the 
 night.\n\nFaraz Niafattah is one of Toronto's most dependable crowd favou
 rites\, known for his bone-dry\, painfully relatable style\, deadpan deli
 very and colourful choice of words. He performs regularly at Yuk Yuk's\, 
 Absolute Comedy and The Corner Comedy Club. He has performed at Just for 
 Laughs Toronto and SF Sketchfest\, been featured at the Vail and Limeston
 e comedy festivals\, and appeared on CBC's LOL network.\n\nThe Boardroom 
 is an intimate club\, so every seat is close to the stage and seats go fa
 st.\n\nDoors 6:30 PM | Show 7:00 PM. Ages 19+. Tickets from $37.61. Right
  on the 512 St. Clair streetcar line.
CATEGORIES:Comedy,The-Boardroom-Comedy-Club
