SUMMARY: Long Winter 15.2 w/ Leona Hell / Lamzy Divey / Hysteria / Clovis
  Consort / Charelle Jazmin / Ksenija Spasic / with visuals by Jason Ball
DESCRIPTION:On December 5\, Long Winter heads back to Kensington Market f
 or another round at St. Stephen-in-the-Fields. It’s the end of the year\,
  so we’re making it count and conjuring a visceral vortex for you to lose
  yourself to. Channel catharsis and step into the body horror noise rock 
 spectacle of Leona Hell or the resistance frequencies of Xicada and Xodka
 ar’s industrial electronic collaboration Hysteria\, rest your heart on lo
 cal emo super group Lamzy Divey (FKA Prior Things\, featuring members of 
 Terry Green\, A Horse Named Friday)\, get sucked into the deep cosmic fre
 e jazz swirl of Clovis Consort\, or get wrapped up in the fluorescent mag
 ic of Ksenija Spasic’s soft sculpture ‘The Breath.’\n\n\nTickets are $20 
 (NOTAFLOF)\, with advance tickets available through Zeffy https://www.zef
 fy.com/en-CA/ticketing/long-winter-152-leona-hell-hysteria-clovis-consort
 -more-tba and more available at the door. Come celebrate 15 years of Long
  Winter with us!\n\n\nFull lineup and event information below!\n\n\nLONG 
 WINTER 15.2\n\nSaturday\, December 5\, 2026\n\nDoors at 8PM\, Music at 8P
 M\n\nLocation: St. Stephen’s\n\n103 Bellevue Ave. Toronto\, ON\n\nALL-AGE
 S / LICENSED\n\n$20 (NOTAFLOF)\n\nAdvance tickets:\n\nhttps://www.zeffy.c
 om/en-CA/ticketing/long-winter-152-leona-hell-hysteria-clovis-consort-mor
 e-tba https://www.zeffy.com/en-CA/ticketing/long-winter-152-leona-hell-hy
 steria-clovis-consort-more-tba\n\n\nFULL LINEUP:\n\nMUSIC:\n\nLeona Hell\
 n\nLamzy Divey\n\nHysteria\n\nClovis Consort\n\n\nART:\n\nCharelle Jazmin
 \n\nKsenija Spasic\n\nwith visuals by Jason Ball\n\n\nVENUE ACCESSIBILITY
 :\n\nThe Church of St. Stephen-in-the-Fields is an accessible space\, wit
 h ramped entry at the rear of the building. Washrooms are all-gender\, in
 cluding an accessible washroom. The venue can be easily accessed by foot\
 , TTC and bicycle lanes. There is no venue-specific parking\, but street 
 parking is available on College\, Bellevue\, Augusta\, Oxford\, and throu
 ghout the surrounding area. For accommodation requests\, please contact u
 s at contact@torontolongwinter.com mailto:contact@torontolongwinter.com\n
 \n\nMASKING ENCOURAGED:\n\nCold season sucks\, and so does COVID. Please 
 consider wearing a mask to this event. If you aren’t feeling well\, stay 
 home! WE TAKE CARE OF US.\n\n\nSUPPORT:\n\nVery special thanks to the Chu
 rch of St. Stephen-in-the-Fields and our beverage sponsor\, Collective Ar
 ts. This event is made possible through the generous support of Toronto A
 rts Council and the Department of Canadian Heritage.
CATEGORIES:Concert,Punk-Rock-Music,St.-Stephen-In-The-Fields,Art-Show/Gal
 lery-Event
