SUMMARY: The Music Gallery & The Ministry of Phonic Services presents Dev
 in DiSanto\, Anne-F Jacques\, Shadow Pattern + Installation by Tümmler St
 udio
DESCRIPTION:Join us at Friends House for an evening of exploratory sound 
 art performance\, in a triple-bill bringing together distinct builders of
  the form—Devin DiSanto\, Anne-F Jacques\, and Shadow Pattern\, featuring
  installation art by Izzy Mink of Tümmler Studio.\n\nStringing together s
 onic elements of the everyday into ideations and completions of tasks\, D
 evin DiSanto visits from New York\, pushing the conceptual bounds of how 
 electroacoustic sounds are created and performed.\n\nWe are also joined b
 y the acute material tinkerings of Anne-F Jacques (Montréal) and the pain
 t-stripped tape ripples of Shadow Pattern (Hamilton)\, for a night of thr
 ee subtle solo sets bridging active listening with experimental performan
 ce.\n\nAs a textural complement to the live sets\, the evening will also 
 feature the installation ‘Persistent Feeder’\, by Izzy Mink of Tümmler St
 udio.\n\nCo-presented and curated by the Ministry of Phonic Services\, a 
 Toronto-based concert presenter and experimental record label.\n\nIf cost
  is a barrier\, please reach out to us at sara@musicgallery.org mailto:sa
 ra@musicgallery.org to reserve a lower-priced PWYC ticket at the door. No
  one will be turned away for lack of funds (NOTAFLOF).
CATEGORIES:Concert,Experimental-Music,The-Music-Gallery,Friends-House
