SUMMARY: Tranzac New Years Eve with Polmo Polpo\, Demon Sweat (all-star W
 een tribute ft. The Marker Starling Band)\, Man Made Hill\, DJs Raf Reza 
 & trustfall
DESCRIPTION:Tranzac New Years Eve 26/27 with:\nPolmo Polpo\nDemon Sweat\n
 Man Made Hill\nDJs Raf Reza & trustfall\n+ Fairweather Tap Takeover\n\n$3
 0 adv / $35 door\n\nPOLMO POLPO is the solo electronic moniker of Sandro 
 Perri exhumed and reimagined for this special one-night only appearance. 
 Hovering around the 25 year anniversary of his debut in the avant-techno 
 realm\, expect dancefloor slush and grit for his post midnight set - his 
 first in 15+ years!\n\nDEMON SWEAT is the all-star WEEN tribute everyone 
 has been talking about\, led by an expanded version of Toronto’s own cult
  heroes The Marker Starling Band. A beautifully skewed lineup of guests w
 ill tackle some of the finest and brownest selections from The Pod\, Pure
  Guava\, 12 Golden Country Greats and all your other favourites. You will
  never hear Bodysurfer\, Ryan Driver\, Nick Flanagan\, Jane Inc\, Pat Lef
 ler\, Alex Lukashevsky\, Marker Starling\, Matt McLaren\, Eliza Niemi\, S
 andro Perri\, Andrew Scott and Drew Smith rip through 20+ Ween classics l
 ike you will this evening. If you are down with boognish then you must no
 t miss this.\n\nMAN MADE HILL is the solo project of Hamilton\, Ontario’s
  Randy Gagne has been steadily percolating in the Canadian experimental u
 nderground for the past 20 years. Originating in the basement murk of the
  DIY noise tape scene\, he has thus blossomed into a confusing\, and exci
 ting synth-pop freak! His live offering congeals performance art\, delusi
 onal funk\, and existential comedy into a dank and bewildering physical e
 xperience.\n\nRAF REZA is a Toronto based DJ and producer stitching the s
 onic links between the seemingly unrelated. Raf has touched many corners 
 of Toronto’s music community over the last 10 years. Between curating the
  bins at Standard Time Record Shop and now running his record label Orphi
 c Apparition\, his ears are tuned to music coming from both the local and
  international community. His DJ and Live sets are genre-fluid in nature 
 where tracks flow through a variety of tempos and sonic palettes.\n\nBase
 d in Toronto\, TRUSTFALL is not just a DJ but also an artist\, radio host
 \, and organizer. Known for their eclectic\, left-field selections and od
 dball psychedelia across all genres\, they bring a unique vibe to every s
 et. Recently\, Trustfall has been organizing a bi-monthly event series ca
 lled Freakers Corner at @bampothouse https://www.instagram.com/bampothous
 e/?hl=en with their collective Freakers Union.\n\n
CATEGORIES:Concert,Tranzac,DJ/Club/Rave
